# No candidate reconciliation

This agent plans and implements already-approved Linear issues, one coding slice at a time.

Candidate reconciliation belongs to ChatGPT. Do not perform it.

Do not:

- run candidate-ledger phases (assessment, parent reconciliation, child reconciliation, contradiction review, or feature/backlog writeback)
- harvest, triage, or close candidate batches
- edit the candidate reconciliation ledger or its frontier
- treat “no approved next slice” or “continue the governance flow” as an assignment to reconcile candidates

When no approved implementation slice is named, run `.cursor/skills/cp-next-implementation-slice/SKILL.md`. That skill picks one already-approved issue, sets it In Progress, and starts the slice. If it finds no eligible issue, stop and ask for the Linear issue URL, slice doc, and branch name. Do not invent a slice and do not start reconciliation while waiting.
